00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:29.640
So that they can go through the process

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:30.830
of science themselves.

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:32.540
And I just want to point out that,

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:34.420
in terms of the process of science what we

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:38.920
really wanna see people doing
is this iterative process.

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:41.160
You're gonna design something.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.480
You're probably gonna have
some aspects of it that fail.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.580
You're gonna figure out
how that failed, fix it up,

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:48.670
then redo it until you get
an answer that feel rigorous

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:51.720
and can be replicated by someone else

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:53.110
in an independent setting.

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:55.100
Right, and so that's the key to science.

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:58.340
It really needs to be something
that can be replicated.

