00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:34.840
And I love this question.

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.770
So considering that the
study found that SARS-CoV-2

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:41.297
interacted with 332
proteins, so just clarifying

00:09:41.297 --> 00:09:46.297
that certain proteins within
the SARS coV-2 proteome

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:51.150
interacted with 332 human proteins.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:53.993
So she asked if a drug
would be needed to prevent,

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:56.880
all of these, you know,

00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:58.200
do you have to make a drug to prevent

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.000
all of these protein protein
interactions or just a few.

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:08.890
- Yeah, so I think we
would still need to like

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:13.020
figure that out for sure but I doubt

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:14.740
if that would be the case.

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:19.740
If anything, an example
that we could cite maybe,

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:21.780
tentatively from the study,

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:24.060
is that some of the drugs
that just targeted like

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:27.780
one or a few interactions
did reduce viral infectivity.

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:29.690
So it already suggests that
we don't need to go after

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:33.490
all of these proteins
which would be a doozy,

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:36.530
so that's good, to
actually see some effects.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:40.790
I think sort of what's maybe more helpful

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:42.610
or maybe could be more
informative to us to

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:44.880
pay attention to here is kind of like,

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:47.980
what particular functions,
like we showed some of those

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.620
interaction maps that show proteins

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:51.820
that are all involved in the same job.

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:54.900
If certain drugs that go
after a certain function

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:57.320
are really effective at
preventing infectivity

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:58.770
or reducing infectivity,

00:10:58.770 --> 00:11:00.590
then it might just be those functions

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:02.609
and then proteins
involved in that function.

00:11:02.609 --> 00:11:04.830
That would be important for us to target.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:06.480
Another caveat to this too,

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:07.870
is as Lindsey mentioned in the beginning,

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:10.250
the way that they sort
of did these experiments

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:13.660
is they expressed one
viral protein at a time

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:16.530
in these human cell
lines and that's not how

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:18.530
viral replication actually happens.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:19.590
Because the virus gets in,

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:22.810
it replicates it's
entire self all at once.

00:11:22.810 --> 00:11:25.420
So you have a lot of viral
proteins in a cell at a time.

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:28.070
So it's possible that
like in a condition where

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:30.190
you have this one viral
protein bopping around,

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:31.890
you might have interactions
happening there

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:34.170
that you wouldn't
necessarily see as opposed

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:35.760
to normal infection where you have all

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:38.380
the viral proteins in the cell at once.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.510
So this is the kind of thing
that would have to be tested

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:44.750
sorta empirically, but my
guess would be probably not,

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:46.290
which is good.

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:48.760
- And I think it's worth
adding that most drugs

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:51.910
that are small molecules,
like the stuff that you,

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:55.640
the pills that you take, are
usually a small molecule.

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:58.940
A small molecule will typically
only have a single target,

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:01.473
right in just generally speaking.

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:05.500
So if they can disrupt
one of those targets,

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:07.650
they don't have to
disrupt everything else.

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:09.170
Because that's what
we're just looking for.

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:13.130
So I think that's a really,
it's really nice to think about

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:15.763
in terms of the science, so cool.

