And she stresses it's a
hypothetical question,

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:25.410
but I still think it's a good question

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:28.150
and good to go into about FDA approval.

00:12:28.150 --> 00:12:30.530
So she asks if an existing drug was

00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:34.300
found to help treat COVID-19
and was FDA approved again,

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:36.960
so for that purpose, what
effect could that have

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:38.980
on the people who already use that drug

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:40.880
to help treat other conditions?

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:43.730
Is there a way to produce
medications on larger scale

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:45.030
or are there restrictions?

00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:49.660
- Yeah it's great.

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:50.670
Lindsey do you wanna take this one?

00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:52.760
- Yeah, I guess I'll start.

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:54.450
My real answer is I don't know

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:55.960
what kind of an effect it would have.

00:12:55.960 --> 00:13:00.960
I know it's been pretty,
like in addition too

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:03.220
the news talking a lot about how

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:04.923
chloroquine and hydroxychloroquine,

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:08.700
maybe might treat COVID-19.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:11.360
There's also been a massive
shortage in those drugs

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:14.480
for people who actually need
them to treat other things,

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:16.290
like rheumatoid arthritis or lupus.

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:17.950
And that's a really big problem.

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:22.300
So I don't know the answer to,
if we find a drug that works

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:23.830
how do we mass produce it?

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:26.853
But I do think that's a super
important question to ask.

00:13:30.179 --> 00:13:32.130
- That was my favorite niece Maggie.

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:34.485
So thank you so much for
your wonderful question.

00:13:34.485 --> 00:13:36.735
(laughing)

00:13:39.683 --> 00:13:41.593
Here's a question from Audrie.

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:44.244
I hope I'm pronouncing
your name correctly.

00:13:44.244 --> 00:13:47.710
What evidence do they have
to determine if the drug has

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:51.190
effectively bound to
either that human protein

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:53.280
or to the viral protein to disrupt that

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:54.913
protein-protein interaction?

00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:01.733
- Okay, so for human
proteins generally like,

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:05.450
so the sort of like the first
way that people will kinda

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:07.920
validate drugs to see if
they bind is basically

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:10.850
they'll look for a drug
that disrupts like,

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:11.970
if it's an enzyme,

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:15.270
like a certain reaction
the enzyme participates in.

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:17.310
Or like it will look for just
like the separate proteins

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:18.670
that are both involved in the interaction

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:20.380
and see like if the drug is there,

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.780
does this enzymatic reaction not happen?

00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:24.060
And that would suggest
that the drug is like

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:25.460
preventing it from happening.

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:28.330
Or these two proteins that
we can usually isolate,

00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:30.320
in the way that Lindsey
described while they're

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:32.670
stuck to each other, are they
no longer stuck to each other

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:33.580
when we give the drug?

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:35.040
So there are sorts of like,

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:36.933
that's kind of like the initial pass.

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:40.710
But another way that
people do it is actually,

00:14:40.710 --> 00:14:42.470
and this I'm not super familiar with,

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:45.000
but I've just seen figures of it before.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:48.380
We can do this technique
call x-ray crystallography

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:51.040
that actually lets us see like physically

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:53.040
the protein and the
compound bound together

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:56.500
and sort of verify that
those chemical interactions,

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:58.210
where the compound or the molecule,

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:00.650
I should say is kind of like basically

00:15:00.650 --> 00:15:02.870
filling that binding
pocket in the protein,

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:06.710
like that actually lets us
see that it's truly happening.

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:08.880
But otherwise it's more
kind of like a functional

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:13.070
sort of like, does this
protein do different things

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:15.870
as you would expect it to if
the drug was binding to it.

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:24.450
- Okay so, I think this
question goes back to

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:27.110
what we talked about a
few minutes ago actually

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:29.420
about the giving the drug before or after

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:31.050
the cells were infected with the virus.

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:34.210
But I still let you expand.

00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:36.970
Do you think that some of
these drugs at some point

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:40.300
will be used prophylactically
for the general public

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:42.893
who is not yet infected
to prevent infection.

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:49.261
- Maybe.

00:15:49.261 --> 00:15:51.070
(laughing)

00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:53.530
I think that depends a lot on their other,

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:56.260
what are their side effects they have?

00:15:56.260 --> 00:16:00.070
So that's always something
that, keep in mind

00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:01.200
with regards to the kind of like,

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:02.910
giving drugs for certain indications,

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:04.850
there's always a risk to benefit ratio

00:16:04.850 --> 00:16:06.150
that you have to consider.

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:08.730
Especially if it's a prophylactic.

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:10.920
If that drugs comes with some
pretty harsh side effects

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:12.750
then you might not want to be taking it

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:16.250
just from the off chance that
you might get an infection.

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:18.420
But if you already have the
infection and it's really bad

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:20.630
and there's nothing else, then
you kind of are more willing

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:22.770
to kind of stomach the side effects

00:16:22.770 --> 00:16:24.820
if it will help you get better.

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:27.000
So I think like that could come into play

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.240
in terms of those decisions.

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:32.310
But all of that stuff has
to be tested in trials.

00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:33.653
- Absolutely.
- Yeah.

